# DayKind environment variables. Copy to .env.local and adjust.
# Never commit real values; .env.local is git-ignored. Set these BEFORE
# `npm run build`: the layout's sample banner is decided at build time.

# Where the app reads data from:
#   sample   – invented, clearly labeled, read-only records; no sign-in (default)
#   supabase – private storage with sign-in (see doc/supabase-setup.md)
DAYKIND_DATA_SOURCE=sample

# IANA timezone used to decide what "today" is for the sample data.
DAYKIND_SAMPLE_TIMEZONE=America/Los_Angeles

# --- Supabase mode only ---
# Project URL and publishable (anon) key from Project Settings → API.
# The publishable key is safe for client use; every query is still limited by
# row-level security to the signed-in, allow-listed user. DayKind never needs
# the service-role/secret key — do not put it here.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Comma-separated email(s) allowed to sign in. Others are signed out with a
# message. The database allowlist (daykind_private.allowed_users) is what
# actually blocks access; keep both in sync.
# DAYKIND_ALLOWED_EMAILS=you@example.com

# --- Reminders (optional; Supabase mode only) ---
# Check-in reminders sent by a server-side scheduler, by email and/or browser
# notification. See doc/reminders.md. Needs DAYKIND_APP_URL,
# REMINDER_DISPATCH_SECRET, and at least one complete channel; otherwise
# nothing is sent and Settings says delivery isn't set up.
# Keep real values in the host's environment settings, never in git or chat.
# Public base URL used in email links:
# DAYKIND_APP_URL=https://daykind.example.com
# Bearer secret for /api/reminders/dispatch (32+ random characters). Register
# its SHA-256 hash in daykind_private.dispatch_keys:
# REMINDER_DISPATCH_SECRET=
# Resend API key (sending access only) and a sender on a verified domain:
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# REMINDER_EMAIL_FROM=DayKind <reminders@example.com>
# Browser notifications: generate with `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`.
# The public key is sent to browsers; the private key stays on the server.
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com
